==Scots==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sco|/ɪlk/}}

===Etymology 1===
From the {{der|sco|ang|īlca}}, from {{der|sco|gem-pro|*ilīkaz}}, a compound of {{m|gem-pro|*iz}} and {{m|gem-pro|*-līkaz}} from the noun {{m|gem-pro|*līką||body}}.

Cognate to {{cog|en|ilk}}.

====Adjective====
{{sco-adj|-}}

# The [[same]].

=====Usage notes=====
* Used following a person’s name to show that he lives in a place of the same name, eg ''Johnstone of that ilk'' means ''Johnstone of Johnstone''.

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|sco|enm|ilk}}, from {{der|sco|ang|ġehwylc||each, every}}, equivalent to {{prefix|sco|y|which}}. Merged with Northern {{der|sco|ang|ylc||each}}. More at {{l|en|each}}. (compare the Dutch ''[[elk]]'' - each).

====Determiner====
